# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# audio-studio — environment template
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in this same folder and fill in the key you have:
#
#     cp .env.example .env          # Git Bash / macOS / Linux
#     copy .env.example .env        # cmd.exe
#
# `.env` is gitignored (see `.gitignore`), and it is the only place a key should
# live. It is read by `audio_studio/env.py` from the working directory, its four
# nearest ancestors, or the repository root - so running the studio from this
# folder, from `audio-studio/`, or from either of the sibling studios all find
# this file. A copy in a parent folder (the suite root ships one too) works as
# well; the nearest file to where you run from wins.
#
# A real environment variable always wins over this file. `.env` never overrides
# something already exported, because a key set by CI, a container or a Windows
# user environment variable is a deliberate act and this file might be stale.
#
# This template is next to the studio on purpose: `audio-studio` runs standalone -
# it is not required to sit inside the `web_av_editor` tree - and a checkout of
# just this folder ships everything a run needs, including the shape of `.env`.
#
# ONLY the *validation* pass needs a key at all. Transcription, alignment and
# every emitted caption file (native JSON, Veed master, SRT, VTT) work with none.
# Get a free key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Gemini (the default provider - used by `--validate llm` / the Emphasis pass)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key-here

# Optional aliases. Any one of these is accepted, in this order of preference:
# GEMINI_API_KEY, GOOGLE_API_KEY, GOOGLE_GENAI_API_KEY. Leave them commented out
# unless you already have a variable by that name in your environment.
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_GENAI_API_KEY=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenRouter (an alternative provider, reached over plain HTTPS)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed if you want to run the validator against a non-Gemini model:
#   python -m audio_studio validate out/song.speech.json --validate llm --provider openrouter
# Get a key at https://openrouter.ai/keys
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_KEY=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# * No transcript, no audio and no media file is ever uploaded to a provider. The
#   validation pass sends the *word list as text* and nothing else.
# * The studio records the provider and the model in each artifact's provenance
#   block. It never records the key.
# * If you see "no API key found", the file is not where the studio is looking:
#   run `python -m audio_studio doctor` and read the `validators` line, or put
#   `.env` in this folder beside this template.
